<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jai Vilas Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jai Vilas Palace is a palace in Gwalior, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built in 1874 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayajirao-scindia">Jayajirao Scindia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Gwalior, in a European style mixing Italian, Tuscan and Corinthian elements. Designed by Sir Michael Filose, it is known for its vast durbar hall and huge crystal chandeliers. Part of it is now a museum, while the Scindia family still lives in the rest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jai-vilas-palace.jpg" alt="Jai Vilas Palace" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mohitkjain123 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jai_Vilas_Palace_(_Scindia_Palace).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
